# What is SQL?
subtitle: "What SQL is, and how one short query keeps just the rows and columns you asked for — and in what order the database does it."
tags: ["sql","databases","queries","data","programming"]
teaches: ["concepts/sql-query","skills/select-where"]
thumb: "band \"SELECT runs last\" note \"you write it first\""
voices: {"a":"gemini:Achird | a friendly, clear teacher who enjoys a neat idea"}

## What is SQL?
use: data_table
with:
    data: '{q.ans}'
    columns:
      - name
      - age
    rows:
      - [Misty, 3]
      - [Tiger, 9]
      - [Luna, 1]
    font_size: 28
    box:
      x: 650
      'y': 200
      w: 300
      h: 250
sources:
    - id: sequel
      title: 'SEQUEL: A Structured English Query Language'
      authors: Chamberlin, D. D. & Boyce, R. F.
      year: 1974
      finding: The IBM query language later renamed SQL

